WGET - download a URL
Usage: wget [-O <file>] [-q] <url>

Fetches a URL and writes the response to a file. Without -O the name is
derived from the URL, with non-word characters replaced by underscores.

-O <file>  write to <file> instead of the derived name
-q         print nothing on success

Examples:
  wget https://example.com/index.html
  wget -O motd.txt https://example.com/motd.txt

Notes:
- Downloads land in the current directory, so cd first if you care.
